WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.917
"Mr. Bubbles escaped from prison," Roxy thought.

2
00:00:04.918 --> 00:00:08.654
"I have to help catch him!"

3
00:00:08.655 --> 00:00:10.793
Roxy called to her friends.

4
00:00:10.794 --> 00:00:13.913
"Hey, guys! I'll meet you at school.

5
00:00:13.914 --> 00:00:17.661
I forgot my homework!"

6
00:00:17.662 --> 00:00:20.318
Terrell watched Roxy hurry away.

7
00:00:20.319 --> 00:00:25.311
"Hmm," he said. "I wonder . . ."

8
00:00:25.312 --> 00:00:30.302
He shook his head. "No, she couldn't be."

9
00:00:30.303 --> 00:00:33.894
A moment later Roxy was zooming through the air.

10
00:00:33.895 --> 00:00:38.475
She landed in the Metro City Prison parking lot.

11
00:00:38.476 --> 00:00:41.330
A prison bus lay on its side.

12
00:00:41.331 --> 00:00:44.133
There was a big hole in the fence.

13
00:00:44.134 --> 00:00:46.944
Detective Smith was talking to two guards.

14
00:00:46.945 --> 00:00:49.613
He held a pen and a small notepad.

15
00:00:49.614 --> 00:00:53.314
The guards looked nervous.

16
00:00:53.315 --> 00:00:56.838
Roxy grinned. "Oh no, Detective!

17
00:00:56.839 --> 00:00:59.803
I didn't know you were sent to prison!"

18
00:00:59.804 --> 00:01:02.501
Detective Smith turned to Roxy.

19
00:01:02.502 --> 00:01:05.784
"This is no time for jokes, Rocket Girl.

20
00:01:05.785 --> 00:01:08.494
A very dangerous prisoner escaped."

21
00:01:08.495 --> 00:01:11.122
"I know," Roxy said.

22
00:01:11.123 --> 00:01:13.501
Detective Smith turned back to the guards.

23
00:01:13.502 --> 00:01:18.483
"So tell me about the prisoner. His name is Mr. Bubbles, right?"

24
00:01:18.484 --> 00:01:20.514
One guard nodded.

25
00:01:20.515 --> 00:01:23.488
"He's one of the worst criminals in Metro City.

26
00:01:23.489 --> 00:01:25.729
He's a clown."

27
00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.114
Detective Smith dropped his pen.

28
00:01:28.115 --> 00:01:31.873
"Did you say he's a c-clown?"

29
00:01:31.874 --> 00:01:34.600
"That's right," the guard said.

30
00:01:34.601 --> 00:01:38.091
Detective Smith's face went pale.

31
00:01:38.092 --> 00:01:40.425
Roxy tapped the detective's shoulder.

32
00:01:40.426 --> 00:01:44.117
"Detective, are you okay?"

33
00:01:44.118 --> 00:01:46.815
Detective Smith didn't say anything.

34
00:01:46.816 --> 00:01:48.708
Roxy looked at the guards.

35
00:01:48.709 --> 00:01:52.139
"So how did Mr. Bubbles escape?"

36
00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.122
The female guard shuddered.

37
00:01:54.123 --> 00:01:56.911
"I was leading Mr. Bubbles out of the prison.

38
00:01:56.912 --> 00:02:00.026
We were going to take him to a different prison.

39
00:02:00.027 --> 00:02:05.156
But when I stepped outside, his gang was waiting in the dark.

40
00:02:05.157 --> 00:02:11.124
They grabbed Mr. Bubbles and ran off."

41
00:02:11.125 --> 00:02:13.671
"Who is in his gang?" Roxy asked.

42
00:02:13.672 --> 00:02:16.358
"Did you get a good look at any of them?"

43
00:02:16.359 --> 00:02:19.281
The first guard nodded. "We sure did.

44
00:02:19.282 --> 00:02:23.111
They were clowns too, just like Mr. Bubbles."

45
00:02:23.112 --> 00:02:26.198
"Gulp!" Detective Smith looked ill.

46
00:02:26.199 --> 00:02:30.157
"Detective, what is wrong with you today?" Roxy asked.

47
00:02:30.158 --> 00:02:33.100
"You're acting strange."

48
00:02:33.101 --> 00:02:35.942
Just then the detective's phone rang.

49
00:02:35.943 --> 00:02:39.234
It was in his pocket, but he didn't seem to hear it.

50
00:02:39.235 --> 00:02:41.640
"Detective Smith," Roxy said.

51
00:02:41.641 --> 00:02:46.483
"Your phone is ringing. Are you going to answer it?"

52
00:02:46.484 --> 00:02:49.637
"Huh?" Detective Smith suddenly looked at Roxy.

53
00:02:49.638 --> 00:02:51.994
"Oh! My phone. Right."

54
00:02:51.995 --> 00:02:55.330
The detective pulled his phone from his pocket.

55
00:02:55.331 --> 00:03:01.240
"Hello? What? Oh . . . Um, okay.

56
00:03:01.241 --> 00:03:05.066
We'll, um, go and check it out, I guess."

57
00:03:05.067 --> 00:03:08.520
Detective Smith hung up the phone and looked at Roxy.

58
00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:13.651
"A policeman just spotted a tiny clown car speeding down West Street."

59
00:03:13.652 --> 00:03:16.582
"That must be Mr. Bubbles!" Roxy said.

60
00:03:16.583 --> 00:03:19.282
"We'd better get over there, Detective.

61
00:03:19.283 --> 00:03:27.672
Let's . . . Detective? Where are you?"

